@startuml password-auth-flow
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 6
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF4FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #5B8DB8
  BoxBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
  BoxBorderColor #CCCCCC
  NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  NoteBorderColor #F9A825
}

title Password and Auth Flow

participant "values.yaml\nsplunkConfig.password\nsplunkConfig.passwordKey" as V
participant "validations.yaml\n(render-time)" as VAL
participant "Secret\nkey: <passwordKey>\n+ default.yml" as SEC
participant "environ.py\n(container init)" as ENV
participant "Ansible\nadd_forward_server.yml" as ANS
participant "splunkd\nREST API" as SPLK

V -> VAL : password == "changeme"\nand existingSecret empty?
note right of VAL
  PWD-01: fails helm install with
  explicit error. Skipped when
  existingSecret is set.
end note
VAL --> V : pass

V -> SEC : b64enc(password) stored as key <passwordKey>\n\ndefault.yml:\n  splunk.password: <password>\n  forward_servers: [...]\n  s2s_port: <port>\n  kvstore.disabled: 1

note over SEC
  Mounted at /mnt/splunk-secrets/.
  SPLUNK_DEFAULTS_URL = /mnt/splunk-secrets/default.yml
  (or splunkConfig.defaultsUrl if set).
end note

SEC -> ENV : SPLUNK_PASSWORD env var\n(secretKeyRef key=<passwordKey>)
note right of ENV
  passwordKey controls which
  Secret key is referenced.
  Default: "password".
  Supports existingSecret with
  custom key names.

  Prevents createdefaults.py from
  generating a random override.
end note

SEC -> ANS : Ansible reads default.yml:\nsplunk.password, forward_servers, s2s_port
ENV -> ANS : SPLUNK_DECLARATIVE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=true

note over ANS
  hash-passwd stdout polluted by chown
  warnings on fresh emptyDir/PVCs.
  REST path is reliable for any
  non-default password.
end note

ANS -> SPLK : splunk add forward-server\n<host>:<port> -auth admin:<password>
SPLK --> ANS : outputs.conf written

ANS -> SPLK : REST: set admin password declaratively
SPLK --> ANS : password confirmed, remote login enabled
@enduml
